WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.250 --> 00:00:02.514
One number, set in Mumbai,

2
00:00:02.514 --> 00:00:04.929
can change your home loan instalment and

3
00:00:04.929 --> 00:00:06.961
the interest on your fixed deposit.

4
00:00:06.961 --> 00:00:08.816
It's called the repo rate.

5
00:00:09.216 --> 00:00:10.841
When a bank is short of cash,

6
00:00:10.841 --> 00:00:12.327
it can borrow from the Reserve Bank

7
00:00:12.327 --> 00:00:13.430
for a short time,

8
00:00:13.430 --> 00:00:16.228
giving government bonds as security.

9
00:00:16.228 --> 00:00:17.935
The interest it pays is the repo

10
00:00:17.935 --> 00:00:18.804
rate.

11
00:00:19.204 --> 00:00:21.131
Repo is short for repurchase.

12
00:00:21.131 --> 00:00:22.780
The bank sells bonds to the RBI

13
00:00:22.780 --> 00:00:24.266
and agrees to buy them back,

14
00:00:24.266 --> 00:00:25.866
a loan in disguise.

15
00:00:26.267 --> 00:00:27.962
Raise the repo rate and loans get

16
00:00:27.962 --> 00:00:31.004
costlier, slowing spending and inflation.

17
00:00:31.004 --> 00:00:32.734
Cut it, and loans get cheaper,

18
00:00:32.734 --> 00:00:34.369
giving growth a push.

19
00:00:34.768 --> 00:00:37.194
The repo rate sits in a corridor.

20
00:00:37.194 --> 00:00:38.994
Above it, the marginal standing facility,

21
00:00:38.994 --> 00:00:40.341
the ceiling.

22
00:00:40.341 --> 00:00:42.872
Below it, the standing deposit facility,

23
00:00:42.872 --> 00:00:44.820
where banks park spare cash.

24
00:00:45.221 --> 00:00:47.253
The Monetary Policy Committee sets it,

25
00:00:47.253 --> 00:00:49.726
meeting about every two months.

26
00:00:49.726 --> 00:00:50.689
If the vote is tied,

27
00:00:50.689 --> 00:00:52.208
the Governor decides.

28
00:00:52.608 --> 00:00:54.106
For GS Three and Prelims:

29
00:00:54.106 --> 00:00:55.545
repo is the rate at which the

30
00:00:55.545 --> 00:00:56.904
RBI lends to banks,

31
00:00:56.904 --> 00:00:59.131
the main lever of monetary policy.

